# CA1844 ("override the memory-based ReadAsync/WriteAsync as well as the array-based ones")
# does not apply to the Stream shims in this folder - RentedStream, StreamOverInputStream,
# StreamOverOutputStream and StreamOverRandomAccessStream.
#
# The rule's premise is that a memory-based override can reach the underlying sink without
# going through a byte[]. These shims sit on the WinRT-shaped surface (IInputStream /
# IOutputStream / IRandomAccessStream, and IRentableStream), which is array- and
# IBuffer-based all the way down, so the array overload is where the work has to happen
# either way. Stream's own base implementation of ReadAsync(Memory<byte>, ...) already does
# the best thing available here - MemoryMarshal.TryGetArray and then the array overload with
# no copy, renting from ArrayPool only for the rare non-array-backed Memory<byte> - so an
# override could match it but never beat it, and would only add code to maintain.
#
# Revisit if these shims ever gain a genuinely span-based sink.

[*.cs]
dotnet_diagnostic.CA1844.severity = none
